From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:49:43 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] segacd-tests

A GBA game played after a Sega CD game whose disc was swapped gets the
same input, frame and picture as a GBA only run. A Sega CD game gets the
Mega Drive pad: X and Y reach the game, slot keeps L2 and R2. A disc
resumes as a disc and never as a NES cart with the same name. Slot's
open path gives a disc the per-game backup RAM and no RAM cart, and the
Mega Drive path still gives the core's own default.
---
